      "input": "nums = [1, 4, 3, 2, 5, 2], x = 3",
      "output": "[1, 2, 2, 4, 3, 5]",
      "explanation": "Elements strictly less than 3 are [1, 2, 2]. Elements greater than or equal to 3 are [4, 3, 5]. Combining them while preserving relative order gives [1, 2, 2, 4, 3, 5]."
